From 326fc0535d002f41c02e7ef2aaedfb78cbed9831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:11:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(router): mark the local-first task analysis internal
 with the key the router reads

Red: a-flag-nothing-reads-is-a-flag-that-was-never-set.test.ts
  "NEGATIVE - no production file passes a key the router does not read"
  Received ["intelligent-router.ts:287"].
Culprit: a8ebf2e0 "Route advanced analysis through local-first brain".

Root cause: the new local-first branch of advancedAnalyzeTask passed
`internalCall: true` in the routeToModel context. routeToModel decides
internal-ness only from `context.purpose === 'internal'`; nothing reads
`context.internalCall`, so the analysis was routed as a visible answer
and the intelligence economy (local brain first, Groq last) never applied
to it - the culprit's own intent. The Gemini branch of the same function
already passes `purpose: 'internal'`.

Decision: R. The key is now `purpose: 'internal'`.

Mutation (fixed mutate.py, restore the dead key):
  x NEGATIVE - no production file passes a key the router does not read
  x advanced analysis respects local-first mode... (with the patched
    assertion below applied) Expected substring: "purpose: 'internal',"
  sha256 identical

Known side effect, out of this group: intelligence-economy.test.ts:65
pins the dead spelling (`expect(src).toContain('internalCall: true')`)
and goes red with this fix (22/23). A one-assertion patch asserting
`purpose: 'internal'` on the local-first call is handed to the
coordinator separately; it makes that suite 23/23 again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
---
 api/src/core/llm/intelligent-router.ts | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/api/src/core/llm/intelligent-router.ts b/api/src/core/llm/intelligent-router.ts
index 1b5d69ac..fc7fa3df 100644
--- a/api/src/core/llm/intelligent-router.ts
+++ b/api/src/core/llm/intelligent-router.ts
@@ -284,7 +284,12 @@ Return exactly this JSON structure:
                 undefined,
                 {
                     modelConfig: { provider: 'auto', apiKey: 'auto-mode' },
-                    internalCall: true,
+                    // The router decides «internal» on `purpose` and on nothing
+                    // else — the Gemini branch above already says it this way.
+                    // The `internalCall` key this call used to pass is read by
+                    // no one, so the local-first analysis was routed as if it
+                    // were the visible answer.
+                    purpose: 'internal',
                     engineeringPipeline: true
                 }
             )
